    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60755" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῡμᾰτ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cover with waves</i>, of the wind, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πεδίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, of the land, <i>to be swept by the sea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				9.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				10.16
			</span></i> (metaph.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>rise in waves</i>, of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ θάλασσα κυματωθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.89
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ποταμὸς ἐκυματοῦτο, ὥσπερ θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>VH</u>
					2.30
				</span></i>
			: metaph., of the air when agitated by the voice, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				234
			</span></i>.</div>
